{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1538178-how-to-justify-running-into-dormant-pandorans-at-low-azoth","id":1538178,"title":"How to justify running into dormant Pandorans at low Azoth?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-06T13:51:23-07:00","id":1538178,"title":"How to justify running into dormant Pandorans at low Azoth?","content":"am running a game right now on rpol have a single Azoth 1 Charachter how to justify them accidentally stumbling across a 'neeedle in a haystack'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T15:08:33-07:00","id":1538179,"title":"","content":"At Azoth 1, a Promethean awakens dormant Pandorans in the same building within a minute. Pandorans track sources of Azoth and are spawned by failed attempts to create Prometheans as well as by division from a Pandoran with a full Pyros pool; newly-spawned Pandorans seek out a safe place to undergo chrysalis once they manage to consume any Pyros at all, and a Pandoran in dormancy looks like an ordinary object appropriate to its location.<br /> <br /> Prometheans have an instinctive understanding of pilgrim marks through the Azothic memory, but pilgrim marks in a location can be out of date, particularly if (for example) the last one to use a safe haven was hunted down and consumed by Pandorans who lacked the forethought to leave them alive.<br /> <br /> Dormant Pandorans are also awakened by any Firestorm whose area encompasses them, and Firestorms can be triggered by a number of circumstances, most prominently the Festering of a severe Wasteland, which may given them cause to move to a different location while they are active.<br /> <br /> Perhaps most of a stretch: the existence of Extempore Prometheans implies the existence of spontaneously-generated Pandorans as well, so you may attach a bit of disturbing local lore to some monsters that emerged with the disappearance of a local statue or a mysterious hole in the landscape or an instance of mass human or animal death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T15:24:12-07:00","id":1538180,"title":"","content":"Dormant Pandorans resemble objects of all shapes and sizes. Make them into a piece of jewelry and have an NPC the player cares about inherit it. Maybe even a cremation diamond, whoever &quot;killed&quot; the Pandoran thought they had gotten a valuable occult resource out of it. Since it had not come close to any Pyros since, there was no issue, but things started to change once it was brought near the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T18:25:05-07:00","id":1538182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1538178-how-to-justify-running-into-dormant-pandorans-at-low-azoth?p=1538180#post1538180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dormant Pandorans resemble objects of all shapes and sizes. Make them into a piece of jewelry and have an NPC the player cares about inherit it. Maybe even a cremation diamond, whoever &quot;killed&quot; the Pandoran thought they had gotten a valuable occult resource out of it. Since it had not come close to any Pyros since, there was no issue, but things started to change once it was brought near the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dormancy is a form of camouflage that Pandorans emerge from (granting them Structure equal to their Health) and full Pandorans are Size 4. Stylistically, the object retains some of the features of the Pandoran, with examples provided including statues, pieces of wood, and stones in a hedge wall.<br /> <br /> Cremation diamonds have sizes measures in carats in the low single digits and a carat is 200 milligrams. A typical Pandoran is not hiding as anybody's jewelry \u2014 the Size rules are flexible, but not <i>that</i> flexible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}